A||||2||3400Fiero||How do you get polyurethane bushings out?||||5||
Z||000000||3400Fiero||09-11-2000||09:54 AM||||I have to replace the lower control arm on the drivers side and I need to get my polyurethane bushings out to put in the new one.  Anyone have any ideas how to get them out without destroying them?<P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||09-11-2000||10:56 AM||||I would try using a large c-clamp and a socket just larger than the large side of the bushing. Put the socket over the bushing, and use the c-clamp to push on the smaller end.||||reg||1
Z||000002||coyote||09-11-2000||06:38 PM||||You could also try heating them, be careful all you want to do is expand the metal a little bit.||||reg||1
